1
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:03,860
Chookity? Chookity!Shoot the laser.
Shoot the laser!

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:05,130
What Mooncake
is trying to say here is...

3
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:06,370
Previously on "Final Space"...

4
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:07,370
Avocato's been trying to save

5
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:08,410
his son, Little Cato,

6
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,480
for a long freakin' time,

7
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:12,030
who the Lord Commander
has locked away.

8
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,370
Oh, crap!

9
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:14,750
Gary swore
that he wouldn't rest

10
00:00:14,790 --> 00:00:16,130
until Little Cato
was back home safe,

11
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:18,650
and Gary always keeps his word.

12
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,790
♪♪

13
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:26,370
♪♪

14
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,030
H.U.E.: Four minutes
of oxygen left, Gary.

15
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,720
[ Gary sighs ]

16
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:40,170
Avocato, now would be the time
to appear and scoop me up.

17
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,130
He's not coming, Gary.

18
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:44,750
I'm afraid no one is.

19
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:47,890
H.U.E., what are my chances
that I'm secretly an immortal?

20
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:51,000
Like Zeus, Hercules,
or Octoprime Rex?

21
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:53,000
There is no chance.

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:54,130
I think there's a chance I got

23
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:55,650
an Octoprime Rex thing
going on.

24
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:56,510
Big time.

25
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:59,000
You have absolutely no chance

26
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,750
because Octoprime Rex

27
00:01:00,790 --> 00:01:02,650
is completely fabricated
by you.

28
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,340
If we're talking percentages

29
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:07,130
of me becoming
an eight-sided enhanced T-Rex,

30
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:08,200
what are the odds?

31
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,200
Zero percent.

32
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:12,370
So death it is.

33
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:15,310
[ Alarm beeping ]

34
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:18,550
♪♪

35
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,510
♪♪

36
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:34,440
♪♪

37
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:53,650
[ Device beeping ]

38
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,720
H.U.E.,
can you patch this in?

39
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:56,340
H.U.E.:
Transferring.

40
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:58,170
[ All gasp ] Dad, these are my coordinates.

41
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,170
Come find me.

42
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,480
I mean, at your leisure,

43
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:02,340
but like,
for me preferably fast.

44
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:03,340
That'd be great.

45
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:04,370
Is that your son?

46
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:06,060
Yes.He looks healthy.

47
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,750
I mean, look, yeah,
it looks like -- it looks like

48
00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:09,240
you did a pretty good job
raising the boy.

49
00:02:09,270 --> 00:02:10,580
I mean, it's obvious
he's been bathing.

50
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:12,000
H.U.E.: I've traced
the coordinates

51
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:14,750
to the Udrex System
in Sector 11.

52
00:02:14,790 --> 00:02:17,030
H.U.E., set a course.
Sector 11.

53
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,170
Out of the question!
We've got a breach to close!

54
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,480
H.U.E., Sector 11.
Now!

55
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:23,130
[ Growls ]Stand back.

56
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:24,130
-Ah!
-I get it.

57
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:25,550
He's your son.

58
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:28,000
But a world can end
if we don't close the breach.

59
00:02:28,030 --> 00:02:30,170
You're right.
It is my son.

60
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,550
And we're getting him.[ Gasps ]

61
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,030
Dude!
What the freak?!

62
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,130
Gary, which is it?

63
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:35,200
[ Gasps ]Earth, or his son?

64
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,030
You're going
to have to choose.

65
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:38,480
Remember.
You promised.

66
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:41,200
[ Laughs ]
It's going down!

67
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:43,030
It...is...going...

68
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,650
downtown, y'all![ Guns fire ]

69
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,310
[ Screams ]

70
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:48,170
I've thought on it...

71
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,820
And I choose both.

72
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,340
But first, we need
to save Little Cato.

73
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,000
In the chair!

74
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:56,480
[ Groans ]

75
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:59,480
You're saying your son is worth
the lives of --

76
00:02:59,510 --> 00:03:00,410
Yes.

77
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,370
Is this totally necessary?

78
00:03:02,410 --> 00:03:04,340
Avocato:
KVN, watch her.

79
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:07,030
I can't believe
I trusted you.

80
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:09,680
We're gonna do
both jobs.

81
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:12,340
Hang tight.
We'll be back.

82
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:21,310
You sure you want
to do this?

83
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,680
There's a 99% chance
that this is a trap.

84
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:27,130
Traps are just
open casting calls for heroes.

85
00:03:27,170 --> 00:03:28,820
Plus,
you already tied up Quinn,

86
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:32,130
so there's no real
rebound after that.

87
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,240
You're a good friend.

88
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:34,720
I would've gone
with "great."

89
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:36,480
But whatever.
I'll take...good.

90
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:38,340
What is happening?

91
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:39,890
I think
we're about to hug.

92
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:41,030
Should we?

93
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:44,000
The siren's call
is beckoning us to embrace.

94
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:46,550
We shan't ignore her.

95
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,650
Mmm.

96
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:49,930
Hell, yeah.

97
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,820
Thanks, bud.
Needed that.

98
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:53,060
Let's get your boy back.

99
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,310
[ Laughs ]
Chookity!

100
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:56,510
Mooncake, we're gonna need

101
00:03:56,550 --> 00:03:58,650
rich sacks of back up.Ooh!

102
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,000
We're goin' down
to the Lord Commander's
prison colony.

103
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:02,550
It's dangerous!Ooh!

104
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,060
It's life-threatening!
We're probably gonna die.

105
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:06,130
[ Whimpers ]I -- you got my back,
little buddy?

106
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:07,820
Chookity!

107
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:10,200
I didn't really sell that
very well, did I?

108
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,240
Crap!
So no back up.

109
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:14,510
Just two hombres
with a dream.

110
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:16,650
H.U.E., let's do this.

111
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:24,370
♪♪

112
00:04:24,410 --> 00:04:25,510
We have arrived.

113
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:26,650
Then land this thing.

114
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:29,000
Unfortunately, if we land,

115
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:30,340
we will be detected.

116
00:04:30,370 --> 00:04:31,720
You'll have to space vault.

117
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,510
Are you sa-- are you saying
we gotta jump?

118
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:35,200
Jump like freakin'
a zillion feet

119
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,510
through
that purple cloud?!

120
00:04:36,550 --> 00:04:37,820
How close
can you get us?

121
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:40,680
Hmm.
Nowhere near close enough.

122
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,890
I can do
nowhere near close enough.

123
00:04:42,930 --> 00:04:45,650
Punch it, H.U.E.!

124
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:49,030
♪♪

125
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:52,240
♪ Oh

126
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:55,510
♪♪

127
00:04:57,510 --> 00:05:00,130
♪ Ooh, ooh-ooh

128
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:03,410
♪♪

129
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,890
[ Music continues in helmet ]What is this?

130
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:06,750
Two planets?!

131
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,480
There's two!
Which one is it?

132
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:10,650
It's left.
Right?

133
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,750
Right?

134
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:13,750
I-I can't hear you
over the music!

135
00:05:13,790 --> 00:05:14,890
Right it is!

136
00:05:14,930 --> 00:05:16,130
Gary!

137
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:17,890
♪♪

138
00:05:17,930 --> 00:05:20,240
♪ Oh, oh

139
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:26,680
♪ Hey

140
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:29,410
[ Music stops ]Something feels wrong.

141
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:31,550
Yeah, because
we're on the wrong planet.

142
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:34,480
Agreed.
This planet is all wrong.

143
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:38,650
No, literally!
We landed on the wrong planet!

144
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:40,000
Gosh dang it.

145
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:41,240
Crap it rough!

146
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:42,510
Of course, it's left.
It's always left.

147
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:44,370
Everything in my life
has always been left.

148
00:05:44,410 --> 00:05:46,440
Left!
Left!

149
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:52,130
KVN: Wup, wup, wup! yum!
Wup, wup, wup!

150
00:05:52,170 --> 00:05:54,340
Quinn:
How does it feel, KVN?

151
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:59,000
To be so hot,
so good looking,

152
00:05:59,030 --> 00:06:03,340
so [Groans]
so handsome?

153
00:06:06,370 --> 00:06:08,750
Hmm.
So, uh, am I

154
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:11,410
the best-looking thing
aboard the Galaxy One?

155
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:12,750
By far.

156
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:14,060
Ohhhhh.

157
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:16,410
Quinn, I can make you
very happy here.

158
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:17,930
Uh,
should I kill Gary?

159
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:20,240
What?!
No.

160
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:22,130
But soon.

161
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:23,750
Then it will just
be the two of us.

162
00:06:23,790 --> 00:06:25,410
And when I say hot,

163
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:28,580
that doesn't even begin to
describe what you've got coming.

164
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,860
Oooooh,
I like it hot!

165
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:34,930
Then you just untie me,
KVN.

166
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:37,240
Maybe I can
re-tie you later?

167
00:06:37,270 --> 00:06:39,000
With love knots?

168
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:40,240
And then I can kill Gary later,
right?

169
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:42,820
Just untie me,
you metallic moron!

170
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,170
Sorry, just to be clear,

171
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,750
did you say kill Gary,
or don't kill Gary?

172
00:06:46,790 --> 00:06:48,240
Shut up.

173
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:51,100
H.U.E., ready a HAWK.
I got a breach to close.

174
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,930
Quinn, you should reconsider.

175
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,820
Too late.
Open the hangar.

176
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,650
Quinn,
I think there is something

177
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,410
you should see before you go.

178
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:02,510
Not interested, H.U.E.
No one left to trust.

179
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:04,340
You can trust Gary.

180
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:05,480
[ Laughs ]

181
00:07:05,510 --> 00:07:07,100
That's a joke, right?

182
00:07:08,410 --> 00:07:09,860
What's this?

183
00:07:09,890 --> 00:07:12,000
It's time you get to know
the real Gary.

184
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:14,890
[ Gasps ]

185
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:16,240
There are hundreds.

186
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,720
Yes, one for every day
of his sentence.

187
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:22,000
Oooh.

188
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:23,650
Hey, Quinn!
It's me, Gary.

189
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,240
[ Chuckles]
Day one!

190
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:27,340
Uh, I should probably start
by apologizing to you

191
00:07:27,370 --> 00:07:29,030
and of course
the Sanchez family

192
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:32,130
for blowing up their very mediocre restaurant.

193
00:07:32,170 --> 00:07:34,550
[ Laughs]
If we're being honest.

194
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:36,130
[ Laughs ]

195
00:07:36,170 --> 00:07:38,750
Looks like we've come down with
a case of wrong-planet-itis.

196
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:40,410
Luckily,
there's a cure.

197
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,510
What?

198
00:07:41,550 --> 00:07:43,410
Jump to the next planet!

199
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:44,580
Aaaah!

200
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:46,580
[ Sighs ]

201
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:48,370
What?
No tunes, baby?!

202
00:07:48,410 --> 00:07:49,930
Whoo!
[ Laughs ]

203
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,060
[ Rock music plays ]Yeah!

204
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,820
We're planet jumping,
man!

205
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:54,200
We are planet jumping!

206
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:58,480
♪♪

207
00:07:58,510 --> 00:07:59,750
[ Music stops ]

208
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:01,820
[ Rocks crumbling ]

209
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:03,750
All right!
Let's kill them all!

210
00:08:03,790 --> 00:08:05,820
[ Laughs ]
Aaaaaaaah!

211
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,680
They're never
gonna see us coming!

212
00:08:10,030 --> 00:08:12,440
[ Panting ]Oh! Whoa! [ Laughs ]

213
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:16,310
I say we burst in,
guns blazing.

214
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:17,930
Blind fire from the hip.

215
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:19,510
For Little Cato.

216
00:08:19,550 --> 00:08:21,000
For Little Cato.

217
00:08:21,030 --> 00:08:22,370
Meow!

218
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:23,930
[ Beeping ]

219
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:27,100
[ Dramatic music plays ]

220
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,370
[ Screaming ]

221
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:43,000
[ Gasps ]
Oh, come on!

222
00:08:43,030 --> 00:08:44,650
Oh, great.
Nobody's around.

223
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,340
This is totally a trap.

224
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:47,240
Where are you going?

225
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:48,510
I gotta take care
of some biz.

226
00:08:48,550 --> 00:08:49,510
Curious?
No.

227
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:50,750
Thought so.

228
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:52,130
I gotta release
a fat pee stream.

229
00:08:52,170 --> 00:08:54,130
I wasn't curious.You were totally curious.

230
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:56,200
No, I wasn't!I -- Whatever!

231
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,060
Little Cato: Papa.

232
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,550
Cato.

233
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:00,750
[ Wings flutter ]

234
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:03,130
Papa.

235
00:09:03,170 --> 00:09:05,060
Papa.

236
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,860
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

237
00:09:06,890 --> 00:09:08,890
[ Electricity crackling ]

238
00:09:10,930 --> 00:09:12,310
[ Distorted scream ]

239
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,510
♪♪

240
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:16,410
Papa.

241
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,410
Little Cato!

242
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,750
Ooh.

243
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:22,340
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm,
not to kill the reunion vibe,

244
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:26,030
but there's something mega
not right with your boy.

245
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:28,680
[ Distorted scream ]

246
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:31,000
It's my fault.
He's angry with me.

247
00:09:31,030 --> 00:09:32,060
Well, it's, uh, you know,
that's great.

248
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:33,480
[ Laughs ]
It's good, it's good.

249
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:36,370
But, uh, he's got a weird way
of showing that,

250
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:40,030
in the fact that
he's hovering off the ground!

251
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,650
Yeah, you got a point.

252
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,860
I got a point?
I know I do.

253
00:09:43,890 --> 00:09:45,650
Aah!
Aah! Agh!

254
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:46,930
Okay,
nice to meet you.

255
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,130
And your name is?

256
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:50,680
Death is sweeter than life.

257
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,650
I don't know
why more kids aren't named

258
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,060
"Death is sweeter
than life."

259
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:56,240
Fine boy
you have here.

260
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,060
Things are about
to get real.

261
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:03,720
You kept your promise,
Gary.

262
00:10:03,750 --> 00:10:05,480
Go back.
Go back to Quinn.

263
00:10:05,510 --> 00:10:06,890
Why would
you even say that?

264
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:08,890
Because -- what do
you really know about me?

265
00:10:08,930 --> 00:10:11,060
I know for a guy who says
he's not a cat,

266
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,170
you sure do love milk.

267
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,550
Other than that,
not a lot.

268
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:17,510
